  "title": "The amplitude by computation",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Exact computation confirming tickets A and C. (1) Census: each of the 2652 isomorphism classes of connected cubic multi-systems with at most 10 points that are not 2-colourable (160 untwisted, 2492 with one twisted incidence; the census of THREEFOLD-GRAMMAR-20261030-001B) is not colourable, has one amplitude at every line, equal to its transpose's at every point and to the product of its brace amplitudes (two-vertex brace and doubled square 1, Heawood 5, planar braces their arborescence number, the one non-planar brace 6). (2) The law: on every three-fold space with at most 22 points (8 classes), at every corner line, the knot's corner relation is exact with lambda(0) = (-1)^(n-1) 5^(Fano atoms); the 24 twisted classes up to 22 points have one amplitude equal to the product of their brace amplitudes. (3) Planar glue: on the omnitruncations of 13 planar maps (up to the dodecahedron, 60 lines) the amplitude at every line equals the number of spanning trees of the map and the three arborescence numbers; on the glue of 6 hypermaps it equals the hypertree count of both hypergraphs (Kalman) and the arborescence numbers, and differs from the spanning-tree count of the hypermap. (4) Trisums: 44 trisums of three prisms along a square face (11 triples, 4 gluings each) and 6 nested trisums are braces with a Pfaffian signing, not colourable with it and colourable without it, with one amplitude shared with the transpose; the amplitude depends on the gluing and is not a function of the pieces' amplitudes ((2,3,3): 13 or 14; (3,3,3): 18 or 21; (4,4,4): 36 or 52), while two cubes and a 2k-prism always give 3k.",
